{
	"version": 5,
	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "EvYVu_GTfysd83oww",
			"description": "Power Armour, Deathwatch Livery",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 4: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 4 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nMechanically identical to the Chapter-issue Mark VII plate it is built from (see that entry's own notes for the black-carapace requirement); the only real difference is cosmetic — the suit is stripped, reforged black and marked with the Deathwatch's silver Chapter-agnostic iconography over the wearer's own Chapter heraldry, per essentially every visual depiction of the Deathwatch in current Codex and Black Library art. A seconded Marine keeps whatever Mark his own Chapter actually issues him; this entry exists only so a Deathwatch character sheet can carry a correctly-named suit without restating the Mark VII stat block. Use the matching include from Imperial Armour.eqp directly (any Mark) for a Marine whose Chapter fields a different pattern.\n\nLore: \"Black plate, silver cross\" is the single most consistent visual signature of the Deathwatch across every source: Codex: Deathwatch, the Deathwatch RPG's cover art and interior illustrations, and Black Library's Deathwatch-focused fiction all describe or depict the same reforging ritual — a Chapter's colours stripped away and replaced with unbroken black and the aquila-and-arrow badge, a visible sign that the wearer now answers to the Long Watch first.\n\nDesign: Deliberately not a new armour entry: the framework and data-format.md both prefer an `include` over restating a DR block that hasn't changed, and nothing about Deathwatch service alters a suit's protection, weak points, or eye-lens DR. Cost is carried over unchanged from the Mark VII entry (the reforging is a Chapter-level or Watch Fortress-level expense assumed already spent before play, not something a player buys again); a GM wanting to price the reforging ritual itself as a one-off Chapter favour can do so narratively without touching this stat block.",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
