			"quantity": 1,
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "eWGsYNGQjeZoenmuh",
					"description": "Auto-senses Suite",
					"local_notes": "Threat auto-cueing, low-light and audio filtering, and passive proximity warning feeding directly into the wearer's helmet display. Requires the black carapace interface to use at full effect.\n\nLore: Depicted throughout Astartes-viewpoint fiction (the Horus Heresy series, Space Marine Battles line) as a constant background hum of tactical data most Astartes barely consciously notice.\n\nDesign: No numeric anchor; modelled as a flat Observation bonus, deliberately larger than the Sororitas suite's, reflecting the fuller sensor package and the neural bandwidth the black carapace provides to use it.",
					"base_value": "6000",
					"base_weight": "4 lb",
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "skill_bonus",
							"selection_type": "skills_with_name",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Observation"
							},
							"amount": 2
						}
					],
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "eZN_AYI8j32QDHB1X",
					"description": "Vox-Link (Integrated)",
					"local_notes": "Squad- and Chapter-band encrypted vox built into the gorget.\n\nLore: Every depiction of Astartes small-unit tactics assumes constant, reliable vox discipline.\n\nDesign: Flavour/utility subsystem; no DR or attribute effect.",
					"base_value": "2000",
					"base_weight": "2 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "eM3z6g-2TW8UBY1Qo",
					"description": "Autoreactive Shoulder Plates",
					"local_notes": "Pauldrons that shift and stiffen a fraction of a second before an incoming blow lands; this reactive behaviour is already folded into the suit's listed arm and torso DR above, not an additional bonus.\n\nLore: A detail repeatedly mentioned in Astartes armour background as part of what makes the suit \"fight with\" its wearer rather than merely cover them.\n\nDesign: Modelled as flavour/explanation for part of the parent item's existing DR rather than a separate bonus, to avoid double-counting protection.",
					"base_value": "3000",
					"base_weight": "8 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "e4XNzmDEdNQO0_Uw_",
					"description": "Respirator & Void Seal",
					"local_notes": "Full atmospheric independence; immune to inhaled toxins and gas while sealed, vacuum-rated for extended operations.\n\nLore: Astartes routinely fight in void war, toxic hive-scum, and daemon-tainted atmospheres in sealed plate across the setting's fiction.\n\nDesign: Standard sealed-armour assumption; no separate anchor.",
					"base_value": "3000",
					"base_weight": "6 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "eNp54LhONR9DCvvyj",
					"description": "Recyclers",
					"local_notes": "Reclaims water and scrubs air, and in conjunction with an Astartes's own physiology allows sealed operation for many days.\n\nLore: Consistent with Astartes physiology background (framework.md notes Astartes \"no need to sleep for weeks\"); the suit's recyclers are the mundane counterpart to that endurance.\n\nDesign: Flavour subsystem, no mechanical bonus.",
					"base_value": "2000",
					"base_weight": "5 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "ejGXEQmcBLqZ38EnX",
					"description": "Servo-Motor Actuators",
					"local_notes": "The bulk of the suit's weight and cost; converts the wearer's black-carapace-transmitted movements into full-body powered assistance.\n\nLore: The core of what makes power armour \"powered\" rather than simple plate, referenced constantly wherever Astartes strength in combat is described.\n\nDesign: ST bonus is the reference figure every other Astartes-pattern suit in this file scales from.",
					"base_value": "14000",
					"base_weight": "65 lb",
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "lifting_st",
							"amount": 9
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "striking_st",
							"amount": 5
						}
					],
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "ea27HoMl_nui8gCSQ",
			"description": "Boltgun, Stalker Pattern (Deathwatch)",
			"local_notes": "Tempest rounds (Special Issue Ammunition) are ballistically the same as the standard subsonic bolt above; their casing is tuned to punch clean through dense natural cover (jungle canopy, fungal growth, a xenos hive-wall's membranous inner layers), so the GM may waive an intervening light-cover DR bonus when one is used against a target behind that kind of obstruction. There is no separate weapon line for them. Stalker Silenced rounds are not listed: this gun's integral suppressor already does what they do.\n\nLore: The Stalker-pattern boltgun is a Deathwatch-specific legacy build: a standard-calibre Astartes boltgun re-machined for a fully semi-automatic-only action, an integral suppressor and subsonic loads, issued to kill-teams that need to put down a target quietly before the rest of a xenos brood notices. Special Issue Ammunition more broadly (Dragonfire and Tempest rounds among them, alongside Kraken, Hellfire, Metal Storm and Vengeance already covered in Boltgun, Godwyn Pattern.eqp) is the Deathwatch RPG line's own signature contribution to boltgun lore; this project's specific division of which round does what is a reasoned approximation built from that line's general design intent, not a verbatim reprint of any single FFG weapon-ammunition table, and no page number is cited because none is confidently known.\n\nDesign: Handling is derived fresh from the Godwyn anchor (Boltgun, Godwyn Pattern.eqp), not copied: same loaded weight class (40 lb, 2 lb over the Godwyn anchor's 38 lb for the suppressor shroud and stiffened barrel a subsonic load needs) and the same min ST 19 the anchor established for a 38-40 lb Astartes-pattern receiver. RoF stays at the Godwyn anchor's 3: the framework rule is RoF 1 only for single-shot or bolt-action mechanisms and RoF 3 for a semi-automatic weapon fired as fast as the trigger allows, and this gun is explicitly the semi-automatic-only pattern (no burst setting). Acc rises to 5 (one over the Godwyn anchor's 4) for the integrated optics a stealth-role weapon needs; Bulk drops one further step to -6 (worse than the Godwyn anchor's -5) for the suppressor's added length. The standard subsonic bolt keeps the Godwyn anchor's full penetrator dice (6dx2(2) pi++ — going quiet doesn't need to cost penetration) but its follow-up shrinks from the anchor's 2d cr ex to 1d+1 cr ex, as on the Primaris Stalker Bolt Rifle, for the same reason (a subsonic round carries less kinetic energy at impact to trigger a full-yield detonation of the internal charge). Dragonfire scales down from the standard round the same way Hellfire does in the Godwyn entry (fewer dice, pi instead of pi++, to make room for payload), but keeps a burn ex follow-up useable against anything flammable rather than Hellfire's organic-only tox follow-up: exact dice distribution, 5dx2(2) pi averages 35 and penetrates carapace (DR 70, eff. DR 35) on 50.0% of hits, Sororitas power armour (DR 85, eff. DR 42.5) on 15.2%, and Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. DR 50) on 1.6% — identical figures to the Godwyn-family Bolt Pistol's own 5dx2(2) line, since it is the same reduced-mass penetrator core in a different housing. Tempest rounds are ballistically unchanged from the standard bolt (6dx2(2) pi++ / 2d cr ex, matching the Godwyn anchor's own 79%/45%/14% figures against carapace/Sororitas/Astartes), so they are folded into the weapon's notes as a cover-penetration rule rather than copied as a second weapon line, the same treatment the Godwyn entry gives Vengeance and Sanctified rounds. Stalker Silenced rounds (a reduced-charge shell for standard boltgun bodies) are omitted: they duplicate what this gun's integral suppressor already does.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes",
				"Deathwatch"
			],
