		{
			"id": "ex-PUO8Pf6gSfz5Eo",
			"description": "Infernus Heavy Bolter",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Infernus pattern is a Deathwatch-specific loadout for the standard heavy bolter, packing a phosphex-and-promethium secondary charge behind each round instead of the usual fragmentation filler — the Deathwatch's answer to swarming, regenerating or bio-armoured xenos (Tyranids above all) where burning a target out matters more than the frag concussion of a standard heavy bolter round.\n\nDesign: The penetrator itself is untouched — identical dice, mechanism and handling to the plain Heavy Bolter (Bolt Weapons.eqp): 85 lb loaded, min ST 14B (mount-borne, not shoulder-borne), RoF 8 per the framework's explicit \"heavy bolter around 8\" rule, Bulk -7 and Rcl 4. Exact dice distribution for the shared penetrator, 7dx2(2) pi++ (avg 49): penetrates carapace (DR 70, eff. DR 35) on 93.9% of hits, Sororitas power armour (DR 85, eff. DR 42.5) on 74.3%, Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. DR 50) on 41.4%, and vehicle AV10 (DR 100) at the same 41.4% while AV11-14 (DR 150-350) fall to 0.1% or less — identical to the plain Heavy Bolter's own figures, since this pattern changes the payload behind a penetrating round, not the round itself. What changes is the follow-up: the Godwyn boltgun's Inferno bolt swaps its standard round's follow-up (a 2d cr ex baseline) for an 8d burn ex incendiary one, and the Infernus does the same over the Heavy Bolter's own larger 2d+2 cr ex follow-up with 10d burn ex, a bigger incendiary punch than the infantry-scale Inferno bolt, in proportion to the bigger case the heavy bolter's own anchor already uses. The burn follow-ups weren't part of the reduction the cr ex bolt cores got, so both stay as they were.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes",
				"Deathwatch"
			],
