		{
			"id": "eK6f0hqJTP5MILz_e",
			"description": "Frag Cannon",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The frag cannon is a Deathwatch signature heavy weapon: a short-ranged, six-shot revolving cannon that throws a devastating cloud of fragmentation at whatever's closest, built specifically for the moment a kill-team is overrun by a Tyranid swarm, an ork mob or a genestealer brood and needs to clear a killing field in front of itself immediately rather than pick targets. Consistently described in Deathwatch-focused background as one of the most destructive close-range weapons an Astartes can carry, at the cost of being all but useless past point-blank range.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor covers this weapon directly, so it's built by doubling the Missile Launcher's own frag-warhead design logic (Heavy Weapons.eqp: \"roughly double the blast and fragmentation dice of a standard hand grenade\" for that launcher's 6d cr ex [6d]) a second time for a purpose-built horde-clearing cannon rather than a general-purpose support weapon: base blast doubled to 6dx2 cr ex (avg 42) while the fragmentation term is dialled back to 4d (avg 14, below the missile launcher's own 6d) since the frag cannon trades blast radius for raw close-range stopping power rather than area denial. It carries no armour divisor and isn't checked against the vehicle AV table, exactly like the missile launcher's own frag load and the mortar in Heavy Weapons.eqp — its entire lore role is infantry and swarm clearance, not armour-killing. Handling: a six-chambered revolving cannon built for an Astartes grip, not a tripod — 50 lb loaded (lighter than the Heavy Bolter's 85 lb, since it has no long barrel or sustained-fire cooling jacket to carry) and min ST 19, matching the Godwyn boltgun anchor's own figure for a similarly Astartes-only handful of a weapon. RoF 1 (one chamber discharged per trigger pull; per the fiction's emphasis on single devastating blasts rather than sustained fire) and Shots 6(5) reflect the six-round cylinder; Bulk -7 and Rcl 3 mark a heavy, hard-kicking weapon that only Astartes-grade strength manages without a mount, matching the Assault Cannon and Heavy Bolter's own Astartes-only handling on this project's heavy-weapons pages.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes",
				"Deathwatch"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "6500",
			"base_weight": "50 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "W3N0Fw8XkrSJ0qDmX",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cr ex",
						"base": "6dx2",
						"fragmentation": "4d",
						"fragmentation_type": "cut"
					},
					"accuracy": "2",
					"range": "15/50",
					"rate_of_fire": "1",
					"shots": "6(5)",
					"bulk": "-7",
					"recoil": "3",
					"strength": "19",
					"usage": "Close-range blast",
					"usage_notes": "No armour divisor: this is a horde/anti-personnel weapon, not an anti-armour one. Treat the bracketed dice as fragmentation per B414, exactly as the Missile Launcher's frag warhead.\n",
					"defaults": [
