		{
			"id": "enZ-CXCWANBtwXPCr",
			"description": "Xenophase Blade",
			"local_notes": "Deliberate relic-tier exception: the phase field ignores armour entirely (armour divisor (inf)), one step beyond the (10) every disruption-field weapon in the framework uses. This is a design escalation for a named archeotech relic, not something the lore requires (canonical Xenophase blades are power-sword-class), and a GM who wants it in line with other power weapons can swap the field-on lines for thr+3d+1(10) imp / sw+3d+1(10) cut.\nPhase field: good for 6 strikes before the generator needs about a minute to recharge (track with the item's Uses counter in GCS, per framework.md's shield-recharge convention); a depleted blade cuts as a plain, beautifully made knife (use the field-off lines) until it recovers.\n\nLore: A rare archeotech or Mechanicus-forged relic entrusted only to a handful of Deathwatch veterans: its blade briefly desynchronises from realspace on impact, letting the edge pass through conventional matter — including armour plate — as if it weren't there, before resynchronising to deliver the cut. Consistently described across Deathwatch background as devastating against otherwise armour-proof xenos and constructs, and consistently rare enough that no kill-team is issued more than one or two.\n\nDesign: Built, not borrowed: no catalogue \"phase weapon\" is copied here. The phasing effect is modelled as Armor Divisor (inf) — the schema's B102-style total bypass of DR — rather than a merely large numeric divisor, because the fiction's claim is a genuine bypass of matter, not \"cuts unusually well\" — a large-but-finite divisor like the disruption-field weapons' (10) would still be stopped cold by a Terminator's DR 200 half the time, which undersells \"passes through armour as if it weren't there.\" What keeps this from being simply the best melee weapon in the game is entirely on the restriction side: a hard six-use limit before the field must recharge (this project's closest existing analogue, the personal force fields in Force Fields.eqp, gate a similar low-single-digits-per-minute budget on a timer rather than a point cost, so the same convention is reused here instead of inventing a new equipment-level limitation field the schema doesn't support) and a very high price/LC0 restricting it to named relics rather than standard-issue kit. Base profile is the plain Astartes Combat Knife/Shortsword baseline (Melee Weapons.eqp: thr+1 imp / sw+1 cut, reach C,1, parry 0) rather than a bigger blade, since the weapon's threat is entirely the phase field, not raw mass — exact odds are unnecessary against DR the weapon is built to ignore, but for reference an Astartes-strength blow at ST 30 (thr 3d, sw 5d+2) averages about 11.5 points on the thrust and 20.5 on the swing before wounding multipliers, so this is a precision, one-target-at-a-time relic, not a way to one-shot a Terminator. The field-off lines give the plain Astartes-scale knife baseline, and the (inf) divisor is a deliberate escalation past the (10) power- field anchor, flagged in the notes. Weight (3 lb) and min ST (11) match a real one-handed long knife; TL12 (archeotech/ STC-era, per the framework's TL table) and LC0 (Astartes/xenos-tech- adjacent relic) are both at the top of their respective brackets.",
